# Q19.2/Q24 (FABLE-SONNET-RECEIVE-RENAME-20260924-166 commit 3, D-48): a repeated declaration's
# own initialiser expression reads whatever occurrence was declared before it, never itself --
# `int: x (x + 2)` after `int: x 1` reads the first x, not the row this statement is creating.
# Registration runs a whole body ahead of emission, so by the time this row's initialiser is
# emitted every occurrence of its name -- including this row itself -- is already in l2_own_n;
# name-only lookup cannot tell "before this row" from "this row". The source-site
# selector also excludes this exact declaration until its candidate is checked/evaluated.
int: l2_own_excl -1
# A probe of the free-name scan (l2_head_read_before): the name it asks about, the statement it ends at, whether
