# K04 (ledger section 57; Codex, FABLE-CODEX-20261004-12): which methods reach each callable formal.
# A fact is written where an actual meets a callable formal (l2_check_call): formal t of the callee
# receives method a (kind 1), the caller's own formal a_fi of method a handed on (kind 2), a node of
# model a that the held name a_fi holds (kind 4), a node a merge builds of model a (kind 5), or an
# occurrence this translation does not follow (kind 3: no route writes it today; a route not yet
# followed has to).  The callee is method `callee`, or, when the call itself goes through a formal,
# whichever method reaches formal via_fi of method via.  The closure (l2_cfr_*) says: method m reaches
# formal t of consumer c, as the unit's occurrence of it or as a node built when the program runs
# (l2_cfr_built); m = -1 says an unfollowed occurrence does.  Compiler metadata: nothing of it exists
# at run time.
# A fact keeps its call site (l2_cfl_node): what one site's actual can denote is asked per site.  The tables
# grow (l2_cfl_reserve, l2_cfr_reserve): no count of facts or of reaching methods is fixed.
@: int l2_cfl_callee 0
@: int l2_cfl_via 0
@: int l2_cfl_via_fi 0
